{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The class-level lookup itself is correctly bypassing instance attributes, and `StopIteration` is scoped around `__next__`. However, the tests currently mask a broken `yield from` iterator contract: plain return values from `send`/`throw` are fed to code that expects `[:yield …]`/`[:return …]` outcomes; the sample happens to produce strings that print but does not verify that yielded values are passed outward correctly. The heap test also compares only two endpoints for dropped generators, not the full graph across repeated suspensions as the ruling requires."}}
